From a1c91674944221e2e910c454ad5d092c5d9b0555 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daliborlol <dalibor@pyro.tf>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:54:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: export the TF2 studio models the exporter rejected

- Accept MDL version 47 (the five TF2 sapper building models). Its
  header layout matches v48; as Studio_ConvertStudioHdrToNewVersion
  does, the v47 zero-frame cache is discarded.
- Sequence layers whose start/peak/tail/end range is NaN (studiomdl
  leaves an addlayer without a range that way: c_ubersaw, c_uberneedle,
  demo_animations, engineer_animations, treasure_hat_oct) no longer fail
  the export. The engine applies such a layer at full weight for the
  whole cycle, which a zero range expresses, so the range is stored as
  zeros with nonFiniteRange: true.
- A bodypart model name that fills its 64-byte field without a
  terminator (tomb_pick_*) is read as the whole field.
- Repairs are listed in the manifest's new warnings array (left out
  when empty) and printed to stderr as "warning: <path>: ...".
- mesh.weights is written only for meshes with morph targets, and empty
  top-level arrays and node.children are left out of the GLB, so
  gltf-validator reports no EMPTY_ENTITY for empty arrays of these kinds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
